  "worked_solution": "First, we express the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(|X|<3)=P(-3<X<3).\n$$\n\nThen, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-3<X<3) & =0.6046 \\\\ 2P(0<X<3) & =0.6046 \\\\ P(0<X<3) & =0.3023 \\\\ P(X<3)-P(X<0) & =0.3023 \\\\ P(X<3)-0.5 & =0.3023 \\\\ P(X<3) & =0.8023 \\\\ P(X\\le 3) & =0.8023\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.8023 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{3-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.8023 \\\\ \u03a6(\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.8023 \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.8023)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\u03a6(0.85)=0.8023\\,\u21d2\\,{\u03a6}^{-1}(0.8023)=0.85.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =0.85 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3}{0.85} \\\\ \\sigma  & \u22483.53.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
